      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    portfolio_returns = [0.02, 0.03, 0.01, -0.01, 0.02, 0.01,\n                         0.03, 0.02, 0.01, 0.02, 0.01, 0.04]\n    market_returns = [0.01, 0.02, 0.02, -0.02, 0.03, 0.02,\n                      0.01, 0.02, 0.03, 0.01, 0.02, 0.03]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    portfolio_mean = sum(portfolio_returns) / len(portfolio_returns)\n    market_mean = sum(market_returns) / len(market_returns)\n\n    covariance = sum(\n        (portfolio_return - portfolio_mean) * (market_return - market_mean)\n        for portfolio_return, market_return in zip(portfolio_returns, market_returns)\n    )\n\n    market_variance = sum(\n        (market_return - market_mean) ** 2\n        for market_return in market_returns\n    )\n\n    beta = covariance / market_variance\n\n    # Return answer rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(beta, 2)\n```",
